**Last commit:** 31d17cf031ecc5bf34e1576491efe6950e1ce437

## Summary

AUR audit detection rules (Task 2 of the AUR security heuristics plan). Added 4 new
aur-audit-adapted detection rules to the PKGBUILD scanner (`pkgbuild_audit.py`):
`pipe_eval_remote` (bash <(curl ...)), `systemd_unit_install` (writing .service/.timer
to absolute systemd paths), `shell_rc_write` (> or tee -a to shell init files, extending
`shell_function_inject`), and `host_tamper` (install/cp writing to absolute system paths
outside $pkgdir). Each rule has metadata in `_RULE_META` with EVERGREEN kind and
aur-audit source attribution. Test class `AurAuditRuleTest` with 8 test methods
(positive + negative cases per rule). Plan: docs/plans/2026-07-16-aur-audit-rules.md.

**Verification:** 330 tests passed (including corpus), benign corpus clean.
